    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0137" n="47" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg47"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1037</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-02-17T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 17,
                                1918, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram January 31.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d70-f1"/> The Secretary of Navy is
                    instructing Admiral Knight to visit Vladivostok to observe conditions and to
                    emphasize friendly attitude this Government has manifested consistently toward
                    people of Russia without regard to parties. Lend him every assistance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
